    <!-- Google Fonts -->
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500&family=Playfair+Display:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        /* All CSS as described above */
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <nav>
            <div class="logo">SYNTHETIC NATURE</div>
            <div class="nav-links">
                <a href="#">EXPLORE</a>
                <a href="#">GALLERY</a>
                <a href="#">ABOUT</a>
                <a href="#">CONTACT</a>
            </div>
        </nav>
        <main>
            <div class="hero-content">
                <h1 class="hero-heading">DISCOVER THE<br>UNSEEN WORLD</h1>
                <p class="hero-subtitle">A journey into miniature natural wonders,<br>captured through art and optics.</p>
                <a href="#" class="hero-btn">ENTER THE EXHIBITION</a>
            </div>
        </main>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## DESIGN NOTES & INTENT

- The overall aesthetic is **minimal, editorial, and gallery-like** — white space and typography do the heavy lifting.
- The color palette is intentionally restrained: near-black text on a warm greige background, with the nature photograph providing all the visual richness on the right side.
- The heading uses a high-contrast serif font (Playfair Display) to evoke an upscale editorial / museum exhibition feel.
- The CTA button is deliberately low-contrast and pill-shaped — it feels like a soft invitation rather than a harsh call to action.
- No JavaScript. No animations. Pure HTML + CSS only.
- No external CSS libraries or utility frameworks.
- The page is a single viewport — no scrolling sections.
