  'Act as an expert frontend developer and UX/UI designer. I need you to create a cinematic, highly interactive, responsive hero section for a portfolio website. All code (HTML, CSS using Tailwind via CDN, and Vanilla JS) must be contained in a single `index.html` file.

Follow these step-by-step instructions exactly:

### Step 1: Base Setup & Typography
- Use Tailwind CSS via CDN.
- Import the ''Inter'' font from Google Fonts and apply it to the body.
- The body should have a dark background (`#0f1012`), white text, and `overflow-x: hidden`.
- Create custom CSS utility classes for tight typography: `.tracking-tightest` (letter-spacing: -0.05em) and `.leading-solid` (line-height: 0.85).

### Step 2: Background Image & Overlays
- Set up a full-screen background container.
- Use this exact image URL for the background: `https://cdn.sceneai.art/Image%20for%20any%20section/c6937ae5-94bb-432c-8cb1-69328c4b4f26.png`
- Apply Tailwind filters to the background image: `grayscale-[20%]` and `contrast-125`.
- Add a gradient overlay container on top of the image to ensure text readability. Use a vertical gradient (dark at top and bottom, transparent in middle) and a horizontal gradient (dark on edges, transparent in middle).
- Ensure the main content wrapper has `max-w-[1440px]` and is horizontally centered (`mx-auto`).

### Step 3: Layout & Content (Responsive)
Create a `main` container covering the full screen with padding. Add the following elements using absolute and flex positioning:
- **Top Header:** Flex row with "LUCAS REIS" (left), "MAIL@REIS.COM" (center), and a small decorative line (right). Text should be tiny (~11px), uppercase, with heavy tracking.
- **Left Sub-header:** Absolute positioned below the header. Text: "Designer <br> Creative Director <br> AI Artist".
- **Right Sub-header:** Absolute positioned below the header on the right. Text: "NEW YORK / <br> 03:09 PM".
- **Main Title:** Absolute positioned at the bottom left. 
  - Left column: A massive "/26" and a tiny subtitle "Selected Projects" below it.
  - Right column: "VISION" and "PORTFOLIO" stacked on top of each other in massive, bold font (up to 160px on desktop), using the tight tracking and solid leading CSS classes.
- **Footer:** Absolute positioned at the bottom. A subtle separator line, followed by "PORTFOLIO" on the left and social links ("X", "LI", "BE") on the right.

### Step 4: Step-by-Step Word Entrance Animation (JavaScript)
- Add a `.split-text` class to all text elements.
- Write a JavaScript script that runs on DOMContentLoaded.
- The script must find all `.split-text` elements, safely split their text into individual words (preserving `<br>` tags and spacing), and wrap each word in two spans: an outer `.word-wrap` (with `overflow: hidden`) and an inner `.word`.
- The `.word` span should start translated down 110% with 0 opacity.
- Apply a globally staggered `transitionDelay` to each word (e.g., `globalIndex * 0.04s`) so every word on the page animates in sequence, one after the other.
- Add an `.animate` class after a short timeout to trigger the words sliding up to 0% translation and 1 opacity.

### Step 5: 3D Mouse Tracking Interaction
- Target the background image container.
- Add CSS properties to the background: `transition: transform 0.15s ease-out;` and a default transform of `perspective(1000px) scale(1.05)` (the scale prevents edges from showing during rotation).
- Write JavaScript to listen for the `mousemove` event across the whole document.
- Calculate the cursor''s X and Y position relative to the center of the window as a percentage (-1 to +1).
- Apply a maximum rotation of 12 degrees.
- Update the background container''s transform to dynamically `rotateX` and `rotateY` based on the cursor position, creating a subtle 3D tilt effect that follows the mouse.
- On `mouseleave`, reset the transform smoothly to 0 degrees.',
