  'https://pub-6e6682d5b928477ab40c1873a1345ec5.r2.dev/videos/1786210961149-es7nne2.mp4',
  '# Recreating the Image Trail Cursor Landing Page

Build a premium landing page with an interactive mouse cursor image trail effect, smooth scrolling, and custom page transitions using Vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. The page features a light theme with clean, minimalist aesthetics, utilizing Google Fonts **Inter** (weights 400-700) and **Instrument Sans**. The page title is "Image Trail Cursor -- High Fidelity Framer Clone".

---

## 🎨 GLOBAL STYLES & RESET
*   **Fonts**: Import and assign `''Inter'', sans-serif` as the primary body font and `''Instrument Sans'', sans-serif` as the secondary font.
*   **Colors**:
    *   Primary Background: `#ffffff`
    *   Secondary Background: `#f5f5f5`
    *   Text Primary: `#000000`
    *   Text Secondary: `#666666`
*   **Global Reset**: Set `box-sizing: border-box`, `margin: 0`, and `padding: 0` on all elements. Enable smooth text rendering and font smoothing (`-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased`).
*   **Wrapper**: Ensure `html` and `body` have `overflow-x: hidden` and default background color `#ffffff`.

---

## 📐 SECTION ORDER & LAYOUT
The landing page consists of three stacked sections aligned vertically:
1.  **Top Section (`.section-top`)**
    *   Background color: `#f5f5f5`
    *   Height: `60vh` (viewport height)
    *   Layout: Centered flexbox column containing the bouncing scroll down indicator.
2.  **Middle Section (`.section-middle`)**
    *   Background color: `#ffffff`
    *   Height: Min-height `100vh` or fixed `800px` height.
    *   Layout: Centered flexbox column with `position: relative` and `overflow: visible` to prevent trail images from clipping at borders.
    *   Contains the hovering text instruction and the `#trail-canvas` overlay.
3.  **Bottom Section (`.section-bottom`)**
    *   Background color: `#f5f5f5`
    *   Height: `80vh`
    *   Layout: Empty viewport placeholder to allow scrolling behavior.

---

## 🧭 SECTION DETAILS

### 1. TOP SECTION (SCROLL INDICATOR)
*   **Down Indicator Container**: A horizontal flex row (`.scroll-down-container`) with a gap of `12px` between elements.
*   **Indicators**:
    *   Left & Right: Arrows "↓" styled with `font-weight: 500`, uppercase, tracking-wider, and responsive size `clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem)`.
    *   Center: Text "Scroll Down" with the same typography and sizing.
*   **Bounce Animation**: The arrows loop in a vertical bounce animation.
    *   Keyframes (`arrow-bounce`): Animate from `transform: translateY(0)` to `transform: translateY(10px)`.
    *   Easing & Timeline: Tween style, duration `1s`, easing `cubic-bezier(0.67, 0.18, 0.32, 1.16)`, repeating infinitely in alternate directions (mirror mode).

### 2. MIDDLE SECTION (INTERACTIVE AREA)
*   **Instruction Text (`.hover-instruction`)**:
    *   Content: "Hover here to see it in action" (lowercase "i" in "it", uppercase "H").
    *   Styling: Font size `clamp(24px, 5vw, 52px)`, `font-weight: 600` (Inter-SemiBold), centered text, max width `600px`, line height `1.2`, letter-spacing `-0.03em`.
    *   Interaction: Set `pointer-events: none` and `z-index: 2` to prevent the text from blocking cursor movements over the trail canvas.
*   **Trail Canvas (`#trail-canvas`)**:
    *   Position: Absolutely pinned to cover 100% width and height of the middle section (`position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;`).
    *   Z-index: `1`
    *   Interaction: Set `pointer-events: auto` to track hover and cursor events.

---

## 🖼️ TRAIL ASSETS (IMAGE BUNDLE)
The image trail uses an ordered list of 10 high-resolution portrait images:
1.  `https://framerusercontent.com/images/Rd8bGKrMA1eRSrfdfP1WKfcqA5k.png?width=448&height=640`
2.  `https://framerusercontent.com/images/7C3SzoyKMzl4gzr2hqKEhD1ciig.png?width=482&height=640`
3.  `https://framerusercontent.com/images/Cpm2FNiKMQUNXtTMcP9BLr8PM.png?width=482&height=640`
4.  `https://framerusercontent.com/images/VOiDIvkkAmPkxFWMl9Ce8l5GlI.png?width=482&height=640`
5.  `https://framerusercontent.com/images/IidhdSMs6KG023K8nWbvaUorWzc.png?width=497&height=640`
6.  `https://framerusercontent.com/images/l26YTzFZWY7F05O83w0S1CARc.png?width=482&height=640`
7.  `https://framerusercontent.com/images/etIiw8oV67pSFiUkDKS5ZNjGs.png?width=482&height=640`
8.  `https://framerusercontent.com/images/8tjkJWz4romEnROuq1QCk6PTB8.png?width=448&height=640`
9.  `https://framerusercontent.com/images/x1PP5Lwqok66irq9EcPfCeZXRw.png?width=512&height=640`
10. `https://framerusercontent.com/images/u3Cd0EMeajt2oQ3uZLkjybkAz4.png?width=426&height=640`

---

## 💫 CSS ANIMATIONS & TRANSITIONS (TRAIL ELEMENTS)
Each trail element consists of an outer wrapper div (`.trail-image-container`) and an inner image element (`.trail-image`).

*   **Outer Wrapper (`.trail-image-container`)**:
    *   Size: Width `220px`, Height `270px` (or via CSS variables `--trail-width`, `--trail-height`).
    *   Position: `position: absolute; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(var(--rotation, 0deg));`
    *   Performance: `pointer-events: none; user-select: none; will-change: transform;`
*   **Inner Image (`.trail-image`)**:
    *   Sizing: `width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 4px; display: block;`
    *   Initial State: `transform: scale(0); opacity: 0;`
    *   **Animate In (`.entering` class)**:
        *   Scale: `transform: scale(1); opacity: 1;`
        *   Transition: Duration `0.75s`, ease curve `cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.46, 0.45, 0.94)` (easeOutQuad). Applies to both transform and opacity.
    *   **Animate Out (`.exiting` class)**:
        *   Scale: `transform: scale(0); opacity: 0;`
        *   Transition: Duration `1.0s`, ease curve `cubic-bezier(0.87, 0, 0.13, 1)` (easeInOutExpo). Applies to both transform and opacity.

---

## ⚙️ JAVASCRIPT STATE ENGINE (`trail.js`)
Implement a class `ImageTrail` that listens to mouse interactions on the canvas container and handles spawning, scrolling, decay timers, and unmounting:

### 1. Configuration Parameters
*   `images`: Array of the 10 image URLs listed above.
*   `imageMode`: `''ordered''` (sequentially loops through the list. A random selection is used only if set to `''random''`).
*   `spawnMode`: `''continuous''` (allows spawning images while the cursor is still).
*   `scrollSpawnMode`: `''distance-gap''` (spawns images during scrolling based on vertical scroll distance).
*   `imageCount`: `35` (maximum images allowed on screen at once; oldest are instantly unmounted if exceeded).
*   `imageLifespan`: `750` (duration in milliseconds each image stays in its active scale state).
*   `removalDelay`: `70` (stagger timeout in milliseconds between sequential image removals).
*   `mouseThreshold`: `100` (distance in pixels the mouse must travel before a new image spawns).
*   `scrollDistanceThreshold`: `80` (scroll distance in pixels required before spawning an image).
*   `idleCursorInterval`: `500` (time interval in milliseconds to spawn a new image when mouse is stationary inside container).
*   `maxRotation`: `25` (maximum tilt angle in degrees, generating random rotations between `-25deg` and `+25deg`).

### 2. Coordinate Calculations & Event Listeners
*   **Mouse Move / Enter**:
    *   Tracks current cursor coordinate: `N.current = { x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY }`.
    *   Computes position relative to canvas container bounding rect: `x = N.current.x - containerRect.left`, `y = N.current.y - containerRect.top`.
    *   Maintains the last spawn coordinate `P.current`. Distance checks verify if Euclidean distance `Math.sqrt((N.x - P.x)^2 + (N.y - P.y)^2) > mouseThreshold`.
    *   Clears a `100ms` move-timeout. If mouse motion stops for longer than `100ms`, the state flag `isCursorMoving` is set to `false`.
*   **Mouse Leave**:
    *   Sets tracking flags to `false`. The engine will stop spawning images.
*   **Scroll Tracking**:
    *   Tracks page scroll offset changes (`window.scrollY`).
    *   When scrolling within the container in `distance-gap` mode:
        *   Accumulates absolute vertical scroll differences: `z.current += Math.abs(currentScrollY - lastScrollY)`.
        *   Once `z.current >= scrollDistanceThreshold`, triggers a scroll-spawn.
        *   **Scroll-Spawn Offset**: Scatter the coordinate `P.current` slightly (`x += (mouseThreshold + 10) * randomDirection`, `y += (mouseThreshold + 10) * randomDirection`) and spawn the image, resetting `P.current` to the current mouse position. This prevents overlapping stacks when scroll coordinates trigger spawning while the mouse is stationary.
        *   Resets the accumulated scroll state `150ms` after scrolling finishes.

### 3. Spawn & Removal Loop (RAF Loop)
Run a continuous loop utilizing `requestAnimationFrame`:
*   **Spawn Check**:
    *   If hovering and moving: Checks if distance exceeds `mouseThreshold`. If yes, spawns an image and sets `P.current = N.current`.
    *   If hovering and stationary (and `spawnMode === ''continuous''`): Checks if time since last spawn is greater than `idleCursorInterval` (500ms). If yes, spawns an image at the current coordinates.
*   **Removal Check**:
    *   Checks if the time since the last staggered removal is greater than or equal to `removalDelay` (70ms).
    *   If yes, and the oldest active image has exceeded its expiration timestamp (`Date.now() >= image.removeTime`):
        *   Pops the oldest image off the queue.
        *   Removes `.entering` and appends `.exiting` to start the scale-out CSS transition.
        *   Sets a timeout equal to the out-transition duration (`1000ms`) to completely remove the element from the DOM.

---

## 🌊 SMOOTH SCROLL INTEGRATION
*   Include the **Lenis** smooth scroll library from a CDN (`https://unpkg.com/lenis@1.1.13/dist/lenis.min.js`).
*   Instantiate Lenis:
    *   Duration: `1.2s`
    *   Easing function: `(t) => Math.min(1, 1.001 - Math.pow(2, -10 * t))` (lerped custom exponential curve).
*   Create a requestAnimationFrame handler to bind Lenis scroll updates on every frame.',
