---

## Procedural 3D Engine & Mathematical Formulas

The 3D gallery is procedurally populated on-demand in a 3D grid. Let the grid block size be \(H = 110\). The camera coordinate in 3D space is tracked.

### 1. Pseudo-Random Generator (PRNG) & Coordinate Hashing
To ensure the infinite environment is deterministic (same seeds generate the same layout of items at coordinates \(cx, cy, cz\)):
- **String Hashing**:
  $$rv(str) = \left| \sum_{i=0}^{len-1} \left( (hash \ll 5) - hash + str.charCodeAt(i) \right) \right| \pmod{2^{32}}$$
- **Sin-Based PRNG**: Given a numeric seed \(e\):
  $$nv(e) = t - \lfloor t \rfloor \quad \text{where} \quad t = \sin(e \cdot 9999) \cdot 10000$$

### 2. Grid Item Generation
Every chunk coordinate tuple \((cx, cy, cz)\) generates \(Q = 5\) mesh items:
- For each item \(a \in [0, Q-1]\), calculate item seed: \(seed = rv(cx + "," + cy + "," + cz) + a \cdot 1000\).
- Compute coordinate offsets using the PRNG:
  $$x = cx \cdot H + nv(seed + 0) \cdot H$$
  $$y = cy \cdot H + nv(seed + 1) \cdot H$$
  $$z = cz \cdot H + nv(seed + 2) \cdot H$$
- Compute item dimensions:
  $$size = 12 + nv(seed + 4) \cdot 8$$
- Compute media index:
  $$mediaIndex = \lfloor nv(seed + 5) \cdot 1,000,000 \rfloor$$

- **Images Pool**: A pool of 9 high-res floral images sourced from a public CDN:
  1. `https://framerusercontent.com/images/BuWrSZ0wmiDkUGZgEJH4eeYdLlA.webp`
  2. `https://framerusercontent.com/images/4NN0VNiOKPV6SOU23LxQfsgpHvE.webp`
  3. `https://framerusercontent.com/images/0p7yUygKZkoFqvQheXhAZtGid0.webp`
  4. `https://framerusercontent.com/images/N6RwntlCipr9rtGkA5DiiC49c.webp`
  5. `https://framerusercontent.com/images/fYJuaiKNu8xnV3bdYHZUM5q6s.webp`
  6. `https://framerusercontent.com/images/D6aPSvfzpqse8NyBozxZyTMHY.webp`
  7. `https://framerusercontent.com/images/k6zlEPFhMGMgP9yRFBGe28UlbyE.webp`
  8. `https://framerusercontent.com/images/mcuO26qFmAYVzvJcyT0ynEiUk.webp`
  9. `https://framerusercontent.com/images/nG24PW5wz1jjRnduO9paSiAWfp8.webp`

- **Texture Auto-Aspect Scaling**:
  When a texture is asynchronously loaded, retrieve the raw image width (\(W_{img}\)) and height (\(H_{img}\)). Adjust the mesh scale dynamically:
  $$scale_x = size \cdot \frac{W_{img}}{H_{img}}, \quad scale_y = size$$

- **Grid Caching (LRU Cache)**:
  Cache the procedural coords array for active grid coordinates using a map (maximum size \(N = 256\)). Evict the least recently used keys when exceeding the limit.

### 3. Infinite Chunk Visibility & Opacity Shader
As the camera moves through the coordinate grid, chunks are loaded and faded.
- **Active Grid Neighborhood**:
  Calculate meshes in active grid cells around the camera. Let active cell radius be \(U = 2\) and fade cell radius be \(W = 1\). Spawns chunks in a relative cube range of \([-3, 3]\) cells in X, Y, Z. Chunks outside this neighborhood are destroyed, disposing of their group meshes and material instances to prevent memory leaks.
- **Interpolated Opacity Calculations**:
  For each mesh in active chunks, compute distance values:
  - Let \(cellDist\) be the Chebyshev distance from the mesh''s home chunk coordinate \((cx, cy, cz)\) to the camera''s current chunk coordinate \((cam_{cx}, cam_{cy}, cam_{cz})\):
    $$cellDist = \max(|cx - cam_{cx}|, |cy - cam_{cy}|, |cz - cam_{cz}|)$$
  - Let \(depthDist = |mesh_z - cam_z|\).
  - If \(depthDist > q + 50\) (where \(q\) is the current fog far limit), set opacity to 0 immediately and set `mesh.visible = false`.
  - Calculate grid boundary falloff:
    $$opacity_{cell} = \begin{cases} 1 & \text{if } cellDist \le U \\ \max\left(0, 1 - \frac{cellDist - U}{W}\right) & \text{if } cellDist > U \end{cases}$$
  - Calculate depth fog boundary falloff (starting at near distance \(K = 140\) up to fog far limit \(q\)):
    $$opacity_{depth} = \begin{cases} 1 & \text{if } depthDist \le K \\ \max\left(0, 1 - \frac{depthDist - K}{q - K}\right) & \text{if } depthDist > K \end{cases}$$
  - Combine opacity:
    $$opacity_{target} = \min(opacity_{cell}, (opacity_{depth})^2)$$
  - Smoothly interpolate the opacity per-frame:
    $$opacity_{new} = lerp(opacity_{old}, opacity_{target}, 0.18)$$
  - If \(opacity_{new} < 0.01\), set to 0. Hide mesh when opacity is 0. If \(opacity_{new} > 0.99\), disable `depthWrite` transparency side-effects by forcing `material.opacity = 1` and `depthWrite = true`.

---

## Interaction Mechanics & Physics Solver

The navigation relies on base coordinates, velocity vectors, target velocities, and a spring-like dampening system.

### 1. Position & Motion Solver
- Base position: \(P = (P_x, P_y, P_z)\), initialized at \((0, 0, 50)\).
- Velocity: \(V = (V_x, V_y, V_z)\), initialized at \((0, 0, 0)\).
- Target Velocity: \(T = (T_x, T_y, T_z)\), initialized at \((0, 0, 0)\).
- Damping (Inertia): Let \(D\) be the damping factor (default `0.16`).
- Friction Decay: Let \(F\) be the decay multiplier (default `0.9`).
- Max Velocity clamp: Let \(G = 3.2\).
- Update steps in the animation loop:
  - Interpolate velocity:
    $$V_{new} = lerp(V_{old}, T_{old}, D)$$
  - Update position:
    $$P_{new} = P_{old} + V_{new}$$
  - Damp target velocity:
    $$T_{new} = T_{old} \cdot F$$
  - Clamp target velocity values to range \([-G, G]\).

### 2. Interaction Bindings & Controls
- **Keyboard Translation**:
  Pressing keys adds acceleration force \(Y = 0.18\) to target velocities:
  - `W` / `ArrowUp`: Forward (\(T_z = T_z - Y\))
  - `S` / `ArrowDown`: Backward (\(T_z = T_z + Y\))
  - `A` / `ArrowLeft`: Left (\(T_x = T_x - Y\))
  - `D` / `ArrowRight`: Right (\(T_x = T_x + Y\))
  - `Q`: Down (\(T_y = T_y - Y\))
  - `E`: Up (\(T_y = T_y + Y\))
- **Mouse Dragging / Touch Panning**:
  Clicking and dragging translates the view.
  - On pointer down, record initial pointer position \(M_0 = (x_0, y_0)\).
  - During drag, calculate delta: \(dx = x - x_0\), \(dy = y - y_0\).
  - Add delta directly to target velocities:
    $$T_x = T_x - dx \cdot 0.025, \quad T_y = T_y + dy \cdot 0.025$$
  - Update \(M_0 = (x, y)\).
  - Touch panning replicates this behavior with touch coordinates (scale factor `0.020`).
- **Mouse Scroll / Pinch-to-Zoom**:
  Scrolling wheel adds zoom force to a scroll accumulator: \(S_{accum} = S_{accum} + \Delta y \cdot scrollIntensity\).
  - On each frame, add accumulator force to target velocity: \(T_z = T_z + S_{accum}\).
  - Decay scroll accumulator: \(S_{accum} = S_{accum} \cdot 0.8\).
  - Pinch zoom translates distance differences \((d_{dist})\) to the accumulator: \(S_{accum} = S_{accum} + (dist_{old} - dist_{new}) \cdot 0.006\).
- **Mouse Drift Parallax**:
  When the user moves the mouse without dragging, apply a subtle parallax drift.
  - Convert mouse coordinates to clip space: \(M_{clip} = (x_{clip}, y_{clip}) \in [-1, 1]\).
  - Compute drift target:
    $$driftFactor = 8 \cdot \max\left(0.3, \min\left(2.0, \frac{P_z}{50}\right)\right)$$
    $$driftTarget = M_{clip} \cdot driftFactor$$
  - Interpolate current drift coordinate towards target:
    $$drift_{new} = lerp(drift_{old}, driftTarget, 0.12)$$
  - Drift is added directly to the camera''s coordinates during rendering:
    $$CameraPosition = P + drift_{current}$$
    *(Drift is bypassed on touch devices or during active drags).*',
  0,
  true,
  259
);
