  'https://pub-6e6682d5b928477ab40c1873a1345ec5.r2.dev/videos/1786215368715-gzpvwtt.mp4',
  '# Orbit Team Section Specification Prompt

This document provides a highly detailed prompt that can be used by an AI assistant to reconstruct the exact Orbit Team Section layout, styling, and interactivity.

***

## System Generation Prompt

Build a premium, interactive **Orbit Team Section** landing page component using Vanilla HTML, CSS (Vanilla CSS), and clean Javascript. The component showcases 11 team members orbiting around a central company brand logo, with interactive hover effects and device-specific responsiveness. The design has a dark-mode tech aesthetic with the font "Inter" (Google Fonts).

### GLOBAL THEME & BACKDROP
- **Background**: Pure dark theme `#030303` set on the body/main wrapper.
- **Backdrop Radial Gradient**: An overlaying backdrop consisting of two layers of radial glows centered behind the component:
  1. `radial-gradient(circle at center, rgba(30, 27, 75, 0.25) 0%, rgba(3, 3, 3, 0) 65%)`
  2. `radial-gradient(circle at center, rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.08) 0%, rgba(3, 3, 3, 0) 45%)`
- **Dot Grid overlay**: A subtle repeating grid using `radial-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.015) 1px, transparent 1px)` with a background size of `24px 24px`.
- **Global Font**: ''Inter'', sans-serif, fallback to system sans-serif.

---

### SECTION LAYOUT & CONCENTRIC ORBITS
The main layout centers around a wrapper container (`.team-orbit-wrapper`) that holds concentric circular rings representing the orbit tracks, the central logo, and the orbiting avatar items.

1. **Size Tokens (Desktop)**:
   - Orbit Wrapper: `600px` width and height.
   - Avatar Cards: `48px` width and height.
   - Central Logo: `20%` of the orbit wrapper size, positioned at the exact center (`top: 50%`, `left: 50%`, `transform: translate(-50%, -50%)`).
2. **Concentric Orbits (Circles)**:
   Three border rings (`.orbit-path`) configured absolutely inside the wrapper:
   - **Orbit 1 (Outer Orbit)**: `100%` of wrapper width/height. Animates **Clockwise** (CW) based on the CSS custom variable `--rotation-angle`.
   - **Orbit 2 (Middle Orbit)**: `75%` of wrapper width/height. Has a solid border of `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12)`. Animates **Counter-Clockwise** (CCW) starting with a `45deg` rotation offset.
   - **Orbit 3 (Inner Orbit)**: `47%` of wrapper width/height. Animates **Clockwise** (CW).

---

### IMAGE AND DATA ASSETS (CDN URLs)
Use these exact public assets for the logos and avatars:
- **Central Logo**: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/NrxXAIF3ckzktuEqvU1GzRf4KY.png?width=256`
- **Orbit 1 (Outer Orbit - 4 Members)**:
  - Liam Brooks: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/N50wEhrokghLB5YTTXJzVI8lYKI.jpg?width=120`
  - Ethan Parker: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/o8ONw6OwXa77Uq96rEahrojqek.jpg?width=120`
  - Sophia Carter: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/VX3qQtLozj4PUti7hmgRnQKDx4.jpg?width=120`
  - Emma Wilson: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/B1iXVXfwBlZ7aUe4w3M6B5sE8.jpg?width=120`
- **Orbit 2 (Middle Orbit - 4 Members)**:
  - Olivia Bennett: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/HKHiJeyAI3A1jzLSu3bwptjjTq0.jpg?width=120`
  - James Foster: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/dLvRZta569u1jdv5oyEG6TkGc.jpg?width=120`
  - Noah Turner: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/QoDpEdcXl1a84eHPrVkBtnPE.jpg?width=120`
  - Ava Mitchell: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/QdrHgLgia2MbIx5g48BR90F9LPY.jpg?width=120`
- **Orbit 3 (Inner Orbit - 3 Members)**:
  - Mia Anderson: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/tWyULVjdjNSHi1BpbJcss2ADP4.jpg?width=120`
  - Lucas Reed: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/nnE1P2fZhh6ih0P0NZSx5g3QSGc.jpg?width=120`
  - Charlotte Davis: `https://framerusercontent.com/images/tjmwpBO6hxnvGMgdwl5nfOkh0.jpg?width=120`

---

### MEMBER AVATAR POSITIONING & ROTATIONS
All orbiting elements are positioned absolutely relative to their parent orbit path circles using percentage-based coordinates and counter-rotations.

1. **Orbit 1 & Orbit 2 Positioning**:
   Positioned at the cardinal directions of the path circles:
   - **Top**: `top: 0; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);`
   - **Right**: `top: 50%; left: 100%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);`
   - **Bottom**: `top: 100%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);`
   - **Left**: `top: 50%; left: 0; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);`

2. **Orbit 3 Spacing (120-degree intervals)**:
   - **Mia Anderson (90°)**: `top: 0; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);`
   - **Lucas Reed (210°)**: `top: 75%; left: 6.7%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);`
   - **Charlotte Davis (330°)**: `top: 75%; left: 93.3%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);`

3. **Keeping Avatars Upright (Counter-Rotations)**:
   As the orbit path rings rotate, the avatars must rotate in the opposite direction at the exact same speed so their faces stay upright relative to the page view:
   - **Orbit 1 and Orbit 3 Items**: Counter-rotate using `rotate(calc(-1 * var(--rotation-angle)))`.
   - **Orbit 2 Items**: Counter-rotate using `rotate(calc(var(--rotation-angle) - 45deg))` to cancel the default 45deg rotation offset of Orbit 2.

---

### INTERACTIVE EFFECTS
1. **Pausing Rotation**:
   Hovering over any avatar (`.orbit-item`) pauses the orbit rotation of all circles instantly and smoothly. When the mouse leaves the avatar, the orbit rotation resumes from the exact position where it was paused.
2. **Avatar Hover States**:
   - **Central Brand Logo**: Remains completely static (no hover scaling or glowing highlights).
   - **Orbit Item Scaling**: The hovered avatar''s wrapper scales up to `1.15` and its border transition speeds up.
   - **Aura Glow Background**: A background element (`.glow-bg`) positioned directly behind the avatar scales to `1.3`, has its opacity set to `1`, and displays a vibrant indigo glow (`rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.4)` background with a `25px` blur box shadow).
   - **Floating Name Labels**: A name tag absolute-positioned underneath the avatar fades in (`opacity: 1`, `visibility: visible`) and slides down to a vertical offset of `calc(avatarSize / 2 + 15px)`.

---

### JAVASCRIPT PHYSICS & VIEWPORT OPTIMIZATIONS
- **rAF Loop**: The rotation logic uses a standard `requestAnimationFrame` loop updating the `--rotation-angle` CSS variable.
- **Delta-Time Calculation**: Compute the time elapsed between frames (`deltaTime` in seconds). Cap the delta time at `0.05` seconds (50ms) to prevent large jumps when changing browser tabs or when performance drops.
- **Speed**: The orbit paths rotate at a constant speed of **10 degrees per second**.
- **Viewport Observer**: Use an `IntersectionObserver` with a `threshold` of `0.05` to monitor the orbit section. Pause the animation frames when the component is scrolled out of view to save battery and CPU cycles.

---

### RESPONSIVE BREAKPOINTS
Use fluid resizing based on viewport width:
- **Tablet (max-width: 900px)**: The orbit wrapper scales down from `600px` to `480px`.
- **Mobile (max-width: 600px)**: 
  - The orbit wrapper scales down to `300px`.
  - The avatar size reduces from `48px` to `32px`.
  - Hover name tags adjust their vertical slide offsets and font-size proportionally (`11px` font-size, `30px` vertical slide-down offset).',
