## 6. User Interaction & Accessibilities
*   **Pointer dragging**: Translates pointer movements on the canvas hit area into scroll offsets, updating velocity.
*   **Mouse wheel scrolling**: Trackpad swipes or scroll wheels update the horizontal displacement force.
*   **Keyboard arrows**: Left and right arrow keys shift the cards horizontally. These keyboard movements are smoothed via GSAP animations.
*   **Adaptive Performance**: Adapts to slower machines. The engine measures performance over a rolling 0.5s interval. If it drops below `46 FPS`, the device pixel ratio (DPR) is lowered in stages from `2.0` down to `1.0` to maintain smooth animations.
*   **Prefers-Reduced-Motion**: Detects system settings automatically. When active, it disables camera parallax, card entrance scaling animations, idle sway movements, and dampens all velocities.
*   **Screen Reader Accessibility**: Screen readers can read the gallery contents from an invisible semantic list matching the current cards:
    ```html
    <ul class="sr-only" aria-label="Gallery topics" id="srList">
      <li>Animals — learn about animals for kids</li>
      <li>History — learn about history for kids</li>
      ...
    </ul>
    ```',
  0,
  true,
  142
);
