  'Build an interactive, high-end 3D Bestseller Book Showcase landing page using Vanilla HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and Three.js (via CDN). The application features a dark, immersive theme with radial gradients, responsive layouts, a floating 3D book display with spring-based physics, procedural textures and cover painters, a custom particle/leaf physics system, and a detailed rating/purchase overlay.

GLOBAL STYLES
- **Background**: Ambient dark blue/navy radial gradient on the body: `radial-gradient(120% 100% at 50% 0%, #1b2246 0%, #141a33 55%, #0f142a 100%)`.
- **Colors**: Set global theme variables:
  - `--navy`: `#141a32` (dark slate navy)
  - `--pink`: `#f591ac` (vibrant pink accent)
  - `--cream`: `#fdfbf4` (warm paper cream)
  - `--lav`: `#c9d0ee` (soft lavender text)
  - `--peri`: `#96a2de` (periwinkle blue accent)
- **Typography**: Clean sans-serif font stack: `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif`.
- **Global Settings**: Fills viewport with `overflow: hidden`, margins and paddings zeroed out, box-sizing set to `border-box`. Focus-visible outlines on buttons set to `2px solid var(--pink)` with `3px` offset.

LAYOUTS AND VIEWMODES
The application operates in two main modes governed by state transitions:
1. **Hero View**: Displays all three books arranged in an elegant, overlapping horizontal fan. A giant "Books" text sits in the background, and navigation sits at the top. Hovering over a book highlights it, lifts it, and spawns an interactive cursor trail.
2. **Detail View**: Focuses on a single selected book. The other books drop out of the frame. The selected book moves to the left (on desktop) or floats in the center (on mobile) and unfolds. A detailed product information panel fades in. A storm of floating leaves fills the canvas around the book, reacting to cursor movement.

1. HERO SECTION & NAV
- **Hero Title**: A massive background fixed word `.hero-word` containing the text "Books". Styled with `font-weight: 800`, letter-spacing `-0.015em`, line-height `0.85`, colored in `--pink`. Sized responsively to `min(22.5vw, 45vh)`. Positioned at `18vh` top, centered.
  - *Animation*: Slides up and fades in on page load (`from: { opacity: 0, transform: translateY(60px) }`). Fades out and slides up (`translateY(-44px)`) when entering Detail View.
- **Navbar**: Fixed container at the top of the viewport with flexbox spacing (`justify-between`, `align-items: center`). Padding: `26px 42px` (reduced to `18px 20px` on mobile/portrait).
  - *Logo*: Text "Bestsellers" on the left, colored in `--pink`, `font-weight: 800`, sized `clamp(20px, 2.2vw, 29px)`.
  - *Action Buttons*: Menu button (`.menu-btn` displaying `=`) and CTA button (`.cta` displaying "Get Tickets"). Both buttons are styled with `--cream` background, `--navy` text, circular or rounded pill shapes, `height: 48px`, and smooth spring scale transition on hover (`transform: scale(1.05)`).
- **Cursor Affordance (`#openBtn`)**: A torn-paper scrap indicator with uppercase text "Open" that trails the mouse cursor using spring-based delay.
  - *Styling*: Styled with a complex clip-path polygon simulating deckled/torn edges, cream gradient background, a repeating linear-gradient paper grain texture overlay, and layered drop-shadows. Fades in only when a book is hovered by a mouse pointer.

2. 3D BOOKS INTERACTION AND PHYSICS
- **Spring Physics**: Create a custom `Spring` class in JavaScript to manage positions (`px`, `py`, `pz`), rotations (`rx`, `ry`, `rz`), scales (`sc`), and hover states (`tiltX`, `tiltY`, `lift`, `cover`, `coverB`, `drag`). Springs use customizable stiffness (default `17` or `120`) and damping (default `6.8` or `14`).
- **Hero Slot Layouts**:
  - *Landscape (Desktop)*:
    - Book 1 (Left): Position `[-2.06, -1.23, -0.12]`, rotation `[-0.045, 0.4, 0.185]`, scale `1.39`
    - Book 2 (Center): Position `[0.3, -1.08, 0.6]`, rotation `[-0.05, -0.1, -0.035]`, scale `1.52`
    - Book 3 (Right): Position `[2.45, -1.41, -0.34]`, rotation `[-0.045, -0.42, -0.17]`, scale `1.39`
  - *Portrait (Mobile)*: Tighter horizontal slots with center book elevated (`[-1.36, -1.0, -0.12]`, `[0.2, -0.45, 0.6]`, `[1.62, -1.1, -0.34]`).
- **Hover Behavior**: Hovering over a book triggers:
  - Lift along Z axis (`s.lift.t = 0.3`).
  - Scale multiplier (`1.09` increase).
  - Subtle positional tilt toward the cursor coordinates (`tiltX`, `tiltY`).
