  'https://pub-6e6682d5b928477ab40c1873a1345ec5.r2.dev/videos/1786374006420-odizg8b.mp4',
  '# Specification for VX — The Printing Roll

Build a 3D interactive portfolio website called **"VX — The Printing Roll"** using standard HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Three.js (r128), and GSAP (3.12.5). The application showcases an endless paper strip unrolling dynamically behind a rolling heavy cylinder. The paper strip prints portfolio pages in its wake, utilizing a single procedural texture atlas, a dynamic ribbon mesh, a custom vertex/fragment shader, a spring-damper motion solver, and an interactive pointer/autopilot steering system.

---

## Global Styles & Page Layout

- **Background**: `#eaeaec` on the root elements (`html`, `body`).
- **Font Family**: `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif`
- **Global Settings**:
  - Full viewport width and height (`100%`).
  - No user scrolling, text selection, or browser-default touch actions: `overflow: hidden`, `touch-action: none`, `user-select: none`, `-webkit-user-select: none`.
  - Box-sizing: `border-box`.
  - Anti-aliased rendering.
- **Stage Canvas (`#stage`)**:
  - `position: fixed`, spanning the entire viewport (`inset: 0`).
  - Default cursor is `grab`; active state is `grabbing`.

---

## HUD (Heads-Up Display) Elements

All HUD elements are fixed on top of the 3D canvas, have `pointer-events: none` disabled, and fade in sequentially with a GSAP stagger effect.

### 1. Brand Logo (`#brand`)
- **Positioning**: Top-left corner (`top: 34px`, `left: 40px`; adjusts to `top: 22px`, `left: 22px` on screens below 720px width).
- **Layout**: Flexbox baseline layout with `gap: 14px`.
- **Inner Elements**:
  - **Mark (`.mark`)**: Text `VX®` (with `sup` for ®). Styled with font size `30px`, weight `800`, letter-spacing `-0.06em`, and `font-style: italic`.
  - **Sub-label (`.sub`)**: Text `Press Division`. Font size `10px`, weight `600`, letter-spacing `0.32em`, uppercase, color `#6a6a6e`.

### 2. Edition Label (`#edition`)
- **Positioning**: Top-right corner (`top: 40px`, `right: 40px`; adjusts to `top: 26px`, `right: 22px` on screens below 720px).
- **Style**: Right-aligned, font size `10px`, weight `600`, letter-spacing `0.28em`, line-height `1.9`, uppercase, color `#6a6a6e`.
- **Text Content**: `Selected works<br /><b>Edition 2019 — 2026</b>` (the bold text uses color `#141414`).

### 3. Page Counter (`#counter`)
- **Positioning**: Bottom-right corner (`bottom: 36px`, `right: 40px`; adjusts to `bottom: 24px`, `right: 22px` on screens below 720px).
- **Style**: Right-aligned.
- **Inner Elements**:
  - **Number (`.num` / `#counterNum`)**: 4-digit formatted integer (e.g., `0000`), font size `40px` (`30px` on mobile), weight `800`, letter-spacing `-0.03em`, tabular numbers representation (`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`), line-height `1`.
  - **Label (`.lbl`)**: Text `Pages printed`. Font size `9px`, weight `600`, letter-spacing `0.32em`, uppercase, color `#6a6a6e`.

### 4. Progress Meter (`#meter`)
- **Positioning**: Bottom-right (`bottom: 108px`, `right: 40px`). Hidden on screens below 720px.
- **Style**: Width `120px`, height `2px`, background `rgba(20, 20, 20, 0.12)`.
- **Inner Fill (`.fill` / `#meterFill`)**: Height `100%`, width dynamically bound to the current page progress percentage (`0%` to `100%`), background color `#141414`, transition `width 0.15s linear`.

### 5. Interactive Hint (`#hint`)
- **Positioning**: Bottom-left (`bottom: 40px`, `left: 40px`; adjusts to `bottom: 28px`, `left: 22px` on screens below 720px).
- **Style**: Font size `10px`, weight `600`, letter-spacing `0.28em` (`0.2em` on mobile), uppercase, color `#6a6a6e`, flexrow align-items center, `gap: 12px`.
- **Dot (`.dot`)**: Width and height `7px`, border-radius `50%`, background `#e4551f`. Animates infinitely with pulse keyframe (`transform: scale(1)` and opacity `1` at 0%/100%, and `transform: scale(1.5)` and opacity `0.45` at 50% over a 1.8s loop). The pulse animation is disabled under `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`.
- **Text (`#hintText`)**: Alternates between:
  - `"Move to steer — click to pause"` (when rolling)
  - `"Paused — click anywhere to resume"` (when paused)

---

## 3D Scene Configuration

- **Renderer**:
  - Antialiased WebGLRenderer.
  - Pixel ratio clamped: `Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2)`.
  - Output encoding: `THREE.sRGBEncoding`.
  - Soft shadows enabled: `THREE.PCFSoftShadowMap`.
- **Scene Fog**: `THREE.Fog(0xeaeaec, 24, 58)`. Matches the renderer clear color.
- **Camera**: Perspective camera with FOV `32`, aspect ratio based on window size, near plane `0.5`, far plane `200`.
- **Lighting**:
  - **Hemisphere Light**: Sky color `#ffffff`, ground color `#d6d6da`, intensity `0.95`.
  - **Directional Sun Light**: Color `#ffffff`, intensity `0.85`. Casts shadows with a map size of `2048x2048`. Shadow camera boundaries: `left: -9`, `right: 9`, `top: 9`, `bottom: -9`, `near: 1`, `far: 40`. Shadow bias: `-0.0004`, normal bias: `0.02`. Sun''s position coordinates and target track the roller''s position in real time (`sun.position.set(pos.x + 5, 10, pos.y + 4)`).
  - **Directional Fill Light**: Color `#ffffff`, intensity `0.22`, positioned at `(-6, 4, -8)`.
- **Floor Plane**:
  - Mesh size: `400 x 400`.
  - Material: `MeshStandardMaterial` with color `#e7e7ea`, roughness `1.0`, metalness `0`.
  - Orientation: Rotated `-Math.PI / 2` on X (aligned to horizontal floor). Receives shadows.

---

## Procedural Textures

All texture assets are rendered on-the-fly inside HTML canvas elements and loaded into Three.js as standard textures using custom random generators to guarantee reproducibility.

### Custom Random Generator (LCG)
To keep the procedural textures consistent across page loads, a Linear Congruential Generator is utilized:
```javascript
var seed = 7;
function rand() {
  seed = (seed * 16807) % 2147483647;
  return (seed - 1) / 2147483646;
}
```

### 1. Canvas Texture Atlas (8 Portfolio Cards)
The atlas canvas has a width of `4096px` (`512px * 8` cells) and height of `512px`.
- **Base Canvas Style**: Fills canvas with a paper color `#f6f5f1`, then draws 2600 random faint fibers using `rgba(120, 116, 105, opacity)` (where opacity ranges from `0.015` to `0.045`).
- **Canvas Draw Helpers**:
  - `bars(x, y, w, n, lh, color)`: Draws `n` text-like rect bars. Each bar''s width is random: `w * (0.55 + rand() * 0.45)` with a line height of `lh` and fill color (defaults to `#c9c8c2`).
  - `label(x, y, txt, color, size)`: Renders text using font weight `700`, custom `size` (default `13px`), and font family `system-ui`.
  - `mono(x, y, txt, color, size)`: Renders text using font weight `600`, custom `size` (default `11px`), and font family `"SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace`.
  - `photo(x, y, w, h, tint)`: Renders an abstract graphic layout. It draws a base rectangle filled with a linear gradient of `tint` colors (`tint[0]` to `tint[1]`). On top of it, 9 blocks of random sizes and positions are blended in using translucent black (`rgba(20,20,22, opacity)`) or translucent white (`rgba(245,244,240, opacity)`) with a top highlight gradient fade.
  - `cardFrame(cx)`: Draws the physical card backing at `cx` offset. Margin is `30px` on all sides (card size: `452px x 452px`). Backing is filled with `#fbfaf7`, given a soft outer shadow (`shadowBlur: 14`, `shadowOffsetY: 3`, `shadowColor: rgba(30, 30, 30, 0.10)`), and bordered with `rgba(20,20,20,0.08)`.
  - `indexTag(f, n)`: Renders the card index in vertical rotated text (e.g. `01/08`) at the bottom right.
- **Card-Specific Layout Designs**:
  - **Card 01 (Editorial)**: Header labels `"VX PRESS"`, `"A/W 26"`. Middle orange block (`#e4551f`) with a large dark circle centered inside it. White bar strip at bottom-left and footer label `"ATELIER 041"`.
  - **Card 02 (B&W Architecture)**: A large photo component rendering a dark vertical gradient (`#3a3a3e` to `#0e0e10`). Below it, header label `"CONCRETE INDEX"`, three lines of text bars, and footer label `"PP. 112 — 139"`.
  - **Card 03 (Typographic)**: Huge italicized text `"VX"` (`128px`, bold, `#161616`) at top left, an orange accent stripe, 7 rows of text bars, and footer label `"MANIFESTO — TEN RULES OF PRINT"`.
  - **Card 04 (Studies Grid)**: Header labels `"STUDIES"`, `"GRID 3×2"`. A 3x2 grid of photos with custom gradient tints (gray, amber, dark-gray, cream, blue, mid-gray). 3 lines of text bars at the bottom.
  - **Card 05 (Sound/Shape)**: Card filled with solid amber (`#f0a32e`). A set of 5 concentric white circular arcs (stroke width `7px`, radii `46px`, `80px`, `114px`, `148px`, `182px`) radiating from the bottom. Dark header label block at top and footer label `"INSTALLATION — HALL B"`.
  - **Card 06 (Device Mockup)**: Blue background strip (`#1e4fd6`) covering the bottom half. Header label `"INTERFACE No.9"` with text bars. A dark device container (`#101014`) floating in the center displaying a light-colored app mock interface. Footer label `"CASE — LEDGER APP"`.
  - **Card 07 (Still Life)**: A centered, clean gray-to-gold gradient photo card block. An accent orange circle (`#e4551f`) positioned at its top right corner. Title `"STILL LIFE, 04"`, text bars, and footer label `"EDITION 2026"`.
  - **Card 08 (Dark Closing Plate)**: A dark-themed card (`#141416`). Contains 6 subtle horizontal lines, an accent orange circle at top right, and huge italic text `"END / LOOP"` (`44px`, white) at bottom left. Footer label `"THE ROLL CONTINUES"`.

### 2. Spiral Cap Texture
Used for the circular sides of the unrolling paper barrel. Renders on a `1024 x 1024` canvas.
- Draws a light base background `#f2f1ec`.
- Generates hundreds of thin concentric circular stroke rings of varying line widths and random opacities (`rgba(112, 110, 102, opacity)`) to simulate layers of rolled paper.
- Draws an overlay spiral cut line using a polar coordinate loop (`turns = 26`) stretching from the inner core to the outer edge.
- Radial gradients apply inner shadow (`rgba(60,58,52,0.32)`) and outer rim shadows (`rgba(60,58,52,0.22)`).

### 3. Roller Contact Blob Shadow Texture
Renders on a `256 x 256` canvas. A simple radial gradient representing a soft contact shadow underneath the roller, transitioning from `#141416` (opacity `0.34` at center, `0.14` at middle, and fading to `0` at the edges).

---

## 3D Roller & Ribbon Geometry

### 1. The Roller Assembly
The roller is a composite group centered at the target coordinate, offset by radius height (`y = 1.75`) off the ground.
- **The Barrel**: A cylinder (`radius: 1.75`, `height: 1.5`, radial segments: `96`, open-ended). Material uses a copy of the canvas atlas texture configured to wrap and offset precisely (`offset.x = 0.25`, `repeat.set(1, 1)`). Casts shadows.
- **Side Caps (L & R)**: Two flat rings (`innerRadius: 1.75 * 0.52`, `outerRadius: 1.75`, radial segments: `96`) placed on each end of the barrel (`x = -0.751` and `x = 0.751`). Uses the spiral cap texture.
- **Inner Core**: A cylinder (`radius: 1.75 * 0.52`, `height: 1.503`, open-ended) made visible from the inside using a double-sided standard gray material (`#dad7cf`).
- **Blob Shadow Plane**: A flat plane (`width: 5.95`, `height: 3.3`) positioned horizontally just above the floor (`y = 0.006`), rotating in sync with the roller''s direction (yaw) to cast a soft ground contact shadow.

### 2. The Ribbon (Unrolling Paper Trail)
An endless paper ribbon mesh built dynamically on every frame to reflect the path traveled by the roller.
- **Geometry Setup**: Uses a `BufferGeometry` with dynamic draw usage (`setUsage(THREE.DynamicDrawUsage)`) containing:
  - `position` array (`Float32Array` of size `(760 + 16 + 2) * 2 * 3`)
  - `normal` array (`Float32Array` of size `(760 + 16 + 2) * 2 * 3`)
  - `uv` array (`Float32Array` of size `(760 + 16 + 2) * 2 * 2`)
  - `aS` (distance coordinate) array (`Float32Array` of size `(760 + 16 + 2) * 2`)
- **Flat Trail Generation**:
  - Iterates through the path history points. Width is standard paper width (`1.5`).
  - To fade the tail out smoothly: the ribbon width tapers to `0` at the very tail (tapering over the first `3.0` units of distance).
  - To prevent overlapping z-fighting: coordinates have an ascending height factor (`y = 0.012 + (s - sTail) * 0.0008`), and the leading segment has an additional lift.
- **The Peel (Curl Geometry)**:
  - Generates a curved bridge mapping from the flat floor surface to the contact tangent of the roller.
  - Peels up along the front of the barrel using a parametric circular arc up to `0.85` radians.
- **Custom Shader Integration**:
  - The ribbon standard material intercepts compiler events (`onBeforeCompile`) to inject attributes and update vertex/fragment code.
  - **Vertex Shader Inject**: Passes the distance value (`aS`) from the geometry attributes down to the fragment shader.
  - **Fragment Shader Inject**: Mixes the texture color with the floor color using a smoothstep transition (`smoothstep(uTailS, uTailS + 3.0, vS)`) based on the current trail end coordinate. This causes the paper trail to dissolve into the floor before its memory budget is recycled.

---

## Math & Motion Physics

The system utilizes an un-clamped physics solver mapping spring-damper equations to steer the roller smoothly.

### 1. Variables & Tuning Constraints
- `RIBBON_W = 1.5` (width of the paper)
- `ROLL_R = 1.75` (roller radius)
- `ATLAS_N = 8` (cards in atlas)
- `CARD_LEN = (2 * Math.PI * ROLL_R) / ATLAS_N` (exactly one page length, ≈ `1.3744` units)
- `REV = 2 * Math.PI * ROLL_R` (one full revolution, ≈ `10.995` units)
- `STEP = 0.12` (distance threshold for pushing a point to path history)
- `MAX_PTS = 760` (trail segment buffer depth)
- `SPRING = 16.0`, `DAMP = 5.4`, `MAX_SPEED = 9.0`

### 2. Motion Step Equations
Each frame, given delta time `dt`:
1. Accelerates towards target coordinate:
   $$\vec{a} = (\vec{p}_{\text{target}} - \vec{p}) \times \text{SPRING} - \vec{v} \times \text{DAMP}$$
2. Updates velocity:
   $$\vec{v} = \vec{v} + \vec{a} \times dt$$
3. Clamps velocity length to `MAX_SPEED`.
4. Moves position:
   $$\vec{p} = \vec{p} + \vec{v} \times dt$$
5. Computes total distance traveled `sTotal` and interpolates orientation `yaw`:
   $$\text{yaw} = \text{angleLerp}(\text{yaw}, \text{atan2}(v_x, v_z), 1 - e^{-7 \times dt})$$
6. Pushes new coordinates to path history rings if displacement exceeds `STEP`.

---

## Interactive Controls & Autopilot

- **Pointer Control**: Intersects cursor position with the ground plane (`y = 0`) using a raycaster. If touch/pointer movement is active, the roller targets this coordinate.
- **Autopilot (Idle Wanderer)**: Activated if no pointer movement is detected for `3200ms`. The target coordinate wanders continuously using time-based sine variations:
  $$\text{autoAngle} = \text{autoAngle} + dt \times (0.34 + 0.5 \sin(\text{time} \times 0.31) + 0.3 \sin(\text{time} \times 0.113 + 2.1))$$
  $$\vec{p}_{\text{target}} = \vec{p} + (\sin(\text{autoAngle}) \times 5.2, \cos(\text{autoAngle}) \times 5.2)$$
- **Click to Pause**: Tapping anywhere toggles state. Uses GSAP to trigger hint transitions.

---

## Setup & Animation Sequence

1. **Pre-roll**: Before rendering the first frame, the physics solver runs `560` step iterations internally. This pre-populates the path history buffers so the roller starts with an established paper trail rather than populating on-screen.
2. **GSAP Intro Timeline**:
   - Zooms camera out smoothly from `1.5` down to `1.0` over `2.2` seconds using `power3.out` easing.
   - Staggers HUD elements fading in from opacity `0` to `1` over `1.2` seconds.
   - Fades out the onboarding gesture hint after `12` seconds.',
  0,
  true,
  221
