- `--duration-press`: `160ms`
- `--duration-chrome`: `180ms`

PAGE ROUTING & FLOW
1. Showroom Landing Page (/) - Renders the main `SupercarShowcase` carousel.
2. Vehicle Detail Page (/vehicles/[id]) - Dynamic route displaying extensive imagery and detailed specs for a specific car.

---

1. SHOWROOM CAROUSEL PAGE
Full viewport size (`width: 100%`, `height: 100svh`), absolute positioning, overflow hidden, using CSS `contain: layout paint;` and `isolation: isolate`.

- Background Layer (`.showroom__bg`): Absolute position filling the viewport, animates `background-color` on car changes. Overlayed with a radial highlight gradient `radial-gradient(circle at 50% 36%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.32), transparent 34%)` and linear-gradient.
- Grain Texture Layer (`.showroom__grain`): Absolute position overlaying the background, applying a subtle radial/linear noise gradient with `opacity: 0.55`.
- Brand Mark (`.brand-mark`): Absolute top-left position. Displays the manufacturer''s logo. Sized using `clamp(50px, 5.6vw, 88px)`. Has dropshadow filter.
- Hamburger Menu (`.hamburger`): Absolute top-right position. A button containing three horizontal spans. Toggling morphs it into an ''X'' using CSS transforms. On hover, the lines shift left.
- Hero Title (`.hero-title`): Absolute centering horizontally, positioned `clamp(92px, 14.8vh, 154px)` from top. Contains manufacturer name (uppercase, `letter-spacing: 0.38em`, `font-weight: 800`) and the car model (uppercase, italic, `font-weight: 900`, `line-height: 0.95`).
- Background Typography (`.background-word`): Positioned absolutely behind the car. A massive, semi-transparent text element (`color: rgba(129, 56, 55, 0.075)`) displaying the model name in all-caps and italic. Sized with `clamp(90px, 15.2vw, 235px)`.
- Hero Car (`.hero-car`): Centered absolutely (`top: 50%; left: 50%; translate3d(-50%, -50%, 0)`). Contains a transparent PNG of the car and an underlying blurry shadow layer (`.hero-car__shadow` using a radial ellipse gradient blurred at `23px`).
- Navigation Arrows (`.arrow-nav`): Left and right arrow buttons centered vertically relative to the carousel controls. Built out of raw CSS elements: a thin line (`.arrow-nav__line`) with a circular dot at one end, and an angled arrow head (`.arrow-nav__head`). On hover, they nudge outwards (`translateX`).
- Read More Button (`.read-more`): Absolute position bottom-right. A white rectangular pill with rounded corners, a subtle box shadow, and a circular outline "+" icon. Clicking links to the detailed `/vehicles/[id]` page.
- Metadata Panel (`.metadata`): Absolute top-right position. Shows the class/category of the vehicle flanked by two thin horizontal border lines.
- Bottom Info Panel (`.info-panel`): Absolute bottom-left position. A white banner wrapping three highlight cards. Has top-right rounded corner (`border-radius: 0 36px 0 0`) and a shadow colored by the dynamic `--panel-shadow`.
- Info Cards (`.info-card`): Displayed as a 3-column grid inside the panel. Each card contains a thumbnail image, an uppercase grey eyebrow, a bold title, and a description. Cards are separated by thin vertical lines. Hovering translates them slightly upwards (`translateY(-3px)`).

---

2. VEHICLE DETAIL PAGE (/vehicles/[id])
Full-viewport layout displaying comprehensive information for a selected car. Dynamic static parameters generated via `generateStaticParams`.

- Back Button (`.vehicle-page__back`): Fixed top-left. Displays the text "Showroom" with an arrow symbol `<` contained in a circular border. Triggers entering slide-up animation.
- Hero Section (`.vehicle-page__hero`): Grid layout splitting the page into two parts:
  - Left column: Manufacturer name, Model name (massive, italic, all-caps, `clamp(54px, 7.5vw, 128px)`), and a description list (`dl`) highlighting the Class and Signature (background word).
  - Right column: Large transparent car image with a heavy drop-shadow and a blurry bottom ellipse shadow.
- Info Cards Section (`.vehicle-page__cards`): A 3-column grid featuring cards with full-width images, an uppercase category label, a bold title, and description text. Cards have a white translucent background and a custom panel shadow.

---

3. GSAP ANIMATIONS & CAROUSEL TRANSITIONS
All transitions on the Showroom homepage coordinate via a GSAP timeline with `CustomEase`.

- Easings:
  - Luxury Ease: `CustomEase.create("luxury-carousel-ease", "0.76,0,0.24,1")`
  - UI Ease Out: `CustomEase.create("luxury-ui-ease-out", "0.23,1,0.32,1")`
- Timings:
  - Car transition: `HERO_DURATION = 0.62`s
  - Title/Manufacturer transition: `TEXT_DURATION = 0.42`s
  - Secondary overlays transition: `SECONDARY_DURATION = 0.36`s
  - Background color tween: `BG_DURATION = 0.55`s
- Transition Offsets:
  - Title counter-parallax movement: `TEXT_DRIFT = 32`px
  - Background Typography movement: `WORD_DRIFT = 48`px
- Mechanism:
  1. The user triggers navigation (Left or Right arrow, or keyboard `ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight`).
  2. The incoming slide layer is mounted dynamically as `is-incoming` with `zIndex: 2`.
  3. Outgoing elements slide in the navigation direction (e.g., car exits to `-75vw` on right navigation, rotating slightly).
  4. Title, background word, and metadata slide in the opposite direction (counter-parallax) to create depth.
  5. Incoming elements translate into view from the opposite direction, snapping to position `0`.
  6. Upon completion, inline GSAP styles are cleared using `clearProps: "transform,opacity,visibility,zIndex,willChange"` to let CSS layout properties take over.
- Image Preloading: An effect pre-caches all vehicle images, logos, and card assets by invoking standard `new Image()` pre-downloads.
- Reduced Motion: Listens to `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` using `useSyncExternalStore`. When active, all GSAP timelines bypass and transition instantly.

