5. RESPONSIVE BREAKPOINTS (MOBILE & TABLET DESIGN)
Layout scales fluidly with media queries using clamp and custom positioning:

- **Desktop (Default)**: Horizontal split layouts. Left-positioned info panels, right-positioned metadata, absolute center titles.
- **Medium Screens (max-width: 1180px)**: Hero car scales to `74vw`. Navigation arrow positions shift slightly. Info panel width shrinks to `min(78vw, 900px)` with tighter margins.
- **Tablet (max-width: 900px)**:
  - Showroom: Read More button floats above the bottom panel (`bottom: 252px`). Background word font sizes adapt (`clamp(74px, 18vw, 150px)`). Navigation arrows lower to `top: 438px`.
  - Info Panel: Collapses into a vertical stack of height `225px` with a single-column grid. Inner dividers are hidden.
  - Detail Page: Back button is pushed up. Hero section converts from a 2-column grid to a single column block layout.
- **Mobile (max-width: 640px)**:
  - Brand logo shrinks to `52px` and hamburger button collapses to `40px` width.
  - Hero title centers with extra side paddings (`72px`) to prevent edge wrapping.
  - Giant background word is sized to `22vw`.
  - Metadata panel is hidden (`display: none`).
  - Read More button moves down (`bottom: 302px`, width `82px`).
  - Navigation arrows are placed at the outer screen edges.
  - Info panel expands to `278px` height with smaller internal paddings.
- **Landscape/Short Viewports (max-height: 760px)**:
  - Adjusts spacing values to fit vertical layouts (e.g., hero title top position, car scale, info panel height limited to `145px`).

